window.docContents[176].resolve({"/LindenstraussPolynomials/DavieGamelin/#mod-doc-LindenstraussPolynomials___DavieGamelin-1-0":{"contents":"Norm preservation \\(Lemma lem:isometry\\)\n\nThe theorem of Davie and Gamelin: for a symmetric n-linear form a and z in the closed unit ball of X^{**},\n|\\overline a(z,\\ldots,z)| \\le \\sup_{\\|x\\|\\le1}|a(x,\\ldots,x)|,\nso the canonical extension preserves the norm of a polynomial.\n\nThe proof follows Davie and Gamelin: points of the unit ball of X are chosen one at a time, by a finite-dimensional form of Goldstine's theorem, so that every increasing tuple of chosen points approximates the iterated extension; the polynomial is then evaluated at averages of the chosen points. It uses only multilinearity, so it works over \\mathbb R as well as over \\mathbb C, as the article remarks.\n\n\n","context":"","header":"LindenstraussPolynomials.DavieGamelin","id":"/LindenstraussPolynomials/DavieGamelin/#mod-doc-LindenstraussPolynomials___DavieGamelin-1-0"}});